25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have a surplus of coders but a dire shortage of phenotyping technicians. The glasshouse crew, however, remains strong.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Shipping costs are rising, but the ministry is still subsidizing glasshouse space. Also, repository deposits are finally moving quickly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks! But the animal facility is accredited and has veterinary cover now.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Field sites are volatile; flooding and fire caused major losses. Interestingly, computation-based projects are far more punctual than those using breeding colonies.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Catalogues have lasting utility, while mechanism studies often stall. Also, computing is now free, but animal rates have spiked.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,That is a worrying gap in technical skill. We should favor projects that don't rely on those missing phenotyping experts.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,"If glasshouse subsidies are holding and the crew is full, perhaps a plant-based study is the safest bet?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"I agree, though we must avoid anything relying on that broken spectroscopy suite.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,And we should certainly avoid live breeding colonies or unstable field sites if we want the project to actually finish.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,The data suggests a catalogue-style project is the most reliable investment for the long term.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,A project that is sustainable in its staffing and infrastructure is a project that will succeed.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Midori,,I feel we are leaning toward something stable and well-supported by the current agency subsidies.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"As long as the facilities can handle it, I'm happy!","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates we avoid the high-risk biological variables Benjamin mentioned.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I am satisfied with the direction. We are prioritizing delivery over theoretical promise.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
